# Financial State Model

Legacy separates financial state into four independent concepts.

```text
Contract
```

Represents the legal agreement.

```text
Salary
```

Represents current annual obligation.

```text
Dead Cap
```

Represents remaining financial obligation after termination.

```text
Future Commitment
```

Represents obligations that have not yet become current.

---

# General Invariants

Every financial event shall satisfy:

1. Every Contract belongs to exactly one Franchise.
2. Every Contract references exactly one Player.
3. Every Contract has one active financial state.
4. Salary cannot become negative.
5. Contract years cannot become negative.
6. Dead Cap cannot exceed remaining obligation.
7. Historical salaries never change.
8. Historical cap calculations remain reproducible.
9. Financial events are immutable.
10. Every cap calculation must be reconstructable from event history.

